From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:55:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: fix the NV2A vertex-shader translator for a
 title's programs

The microcode decoder used field positions that are not the NV2A's
(several overlapped), so no real program decoded. Checked against
Crash Bandicoot: The Wrath of Cortex's programs (twoc notes 18.38):

- Fields as xemu decodes them: DWORD 0 unused, then ILU/MAC ops,
  constant and input indices, three sources (mux, temp, swizzle,
  negate), MAC/ILU temp masks, the output write (mask, bank, address,
  unit) and relative addressing. A paired ILU op writes R1.
- MAC and ILU read before either writes, as they run in parallel.
- The output struct is the pixel shaders' input (PS_IN), so the stages
  link; outputs default to (0, 0, 0, 1).
- oPos comes back from the NV2A's screen space to clip space through
  the XDK's viewport constants c58/c59.
- Every register the program reads is a float4 in the input layout:
  a declaration can put any attribute in any register.
- EXP, LOG, LIT and RCC as the NV2A defines them.

Not upstream: kept in this clone only (twoc notes, rule 18.32).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/d3d/d3d8_vsh.c | 1135 ++++++++++++--------------------------------
 src/d3d/d3d8_vsh.h |   49 +-
 2 files changed, 325 insertions(+), 859 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/d3d/d3d8_vsh.c b/src/d3d/d3d8_vsh.c
index f541428..8161b60 100644
--- a/src/d3d/d3d8_vsh.c
+++ b/src/d3d/d3d8_vsh.c
@@ -12,9 +12,15 @@
  *   5. Cache: hash microcode -> reuse compiled shader on subsequent draws
  *
  * The generated HLSL uses:
- *   - cbuffer at b1: 192 float4 constants (c0-c191)
- *   - Input semantics: ATTR0-ATTR15 mapped to v0-v15
- *   - Output semantics: SV_POSITION, COLOR0/1, TEXCOORD0-3, FOG, PSIZE
+ *   - cbuffer at b1: 192 float4 constants (c0-c191), indexed as the
+ *     microcode indexes them (an XDK title's c0 is slot 96)
+ *   - Input semantics: ATTR0-ATTR15 mapped to v0-v15, each a float4
+ *   - Outputs: the pixel shaders' input struct, with oPos taken from the
+ *     NV2A's screen space back to clip space through c58/c59
+ *
+ * Local fix (twoc notes 18.38): the field layout, the parallel MAC/ILU
+ * semantics, the output struct, the screen-space position and the input
+ * layout were rewritten after checking against a title's programs.
  */
 
